  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "rhythm-dictation",
      "title": "Rhythm Dictation",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** ear-training | **Difficulty:** 3/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Rhythm dictation trains you to notate or reproduce rhythmic patterns heard — essential for learning tunes by ear."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "subdivision",
      "title": "Subdivision",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Feel beat first, then subdivide: eighths in 4/4, triplets in 6/8. Tap foot on main beat only."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "patterns",
      "title": "Patterns",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Start with 2-bar patterns: quarter and eighth combinations. Add syncopation. Jig patterns: long-short-short or three equal eighths per beat."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "notation",
      "title": "Notation",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Use correct beam grouping — eighths beamed per beat in 4/4; in 6/8, beam three eighths per beat."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "practice",
      "title": "Practice",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Clap back rhythms before writing. Slow recordings to 75% speed. Bodhrán and metronome apps help."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
